{
"about": "Esc after a send from the compose box (docs/compose-box.md D18). `cases`: the five times in Patton's main.log (20-22 Nov 2026) he sent from the box, pressed Esc in it (handed to Claude as route pty), and his next send went out joined to the message Claude Code had put back in its bar; offsets in ms from the send, no message text. `recording`: real Claude Code v2.1.321 (classic renderer, 100x30, xterm-256color, hooks and transcripts off, bypass mode) recorded through a pty on 2026-11-22: chunks {t: seconds, b: base64 bytes} with step marks {t, mark} written at the moment the step's keys were sent. Four scenes: single (a one-line message sent, Esc 1.5 s later, Claude puts it back in its bar 79 ms after the Esc, Ctrl+C empties the bar); multi (a 3-line bracketed paste sent, Esc, back as three rows, Ctrl+C empties all of them); foreign (text typed into Claude's own bar, then a line sent after it, Esc: Claude's bar holds both, one row); foreign2 (two lines typed into Claude's bar with backslash-Enter, a line sent after them, Esc: two rows back, Ctrl+C empties them).",
